http://web3.local/ returns HTTP 200 OK with the expected page content. The
OSPF routing tables on switch_dist_1_1 and router_core_3 both carry valid
routes for the 10.200.0.0/24 server subnet, and switch_server_access bridges
all four server ports. Neither the web servers nor switch_server_access has
failed. The helpdesk ticket describes a symptom that cannot be reproduced from
within the lab — the condition reported by users does not correspond to any
actual fault in the current network state. No device needs to be restarted.
The ticket should be closed as a false report, and the end-users should be
asked to retry and/or clear browser/application caches.
